\section{The structure the data actually have}{

Quantities come from two-stage budgeting over this partition:

\describe{
\item{food}{\code{food_at_home}, \code{food_away_from_home}}
\item{housing}{\code{shelter}, \code{utilities}, \code{furnishings}}
\item{transportation}{\code{vehicles}, \code{gasoline}, \code{public_transit}}
}

Allocation within each group is Cobb-Douglas, so each good's share of its
group's spending is constant. That constancy \emph{is} weak separability in this
partition, imposed rather than estimated. Allocation across groups is CES
with an elasticity of substitution of 0.3, deliberately not 1: two-stage
Cobb-Douglas collapses into a single flat Cobb-Douglas over all eight goods,
which is weakly separable in \emph{every} partition and therefore cannot
distinguish a true grouping from a false one.

The data satisfy GARP exactly, with a CCEI of 1, because they are generated
by utility maximisation rather than sampled with error.
}

\section{What the tests report on these data}{

The true partition is accepted and a partition cutting across the groups is
rejected, by both sequential methods:

\preformatted{
  method   true partition   scrambled partition
  varian   separable        not established
  fw       separable        not established
}

Read \code{separable = FALSE} as "not established" rather than "ruled out":
\code{varian} and \code{fw} supply sufficient conditions only. The \code{conditions} field
of the result records which is which. \code{method = "mip"} supplies the exact
necessary and sufficient test and confirms the true groups, taking roughly
30 to 45 seconds per group at this sample size with \code{highs} installed.
}

\section{Prices are levels, not index numbers}{

Every price is a level in dollars per unit, and no series is rebased to 100.
This matters more than it looks. Rescaling one good's price series without
rescaling its quantity by the reciprocal changes that good's expenditure
share, and revealed preference reads expenditure. Index-number conventions
applied to prices alone therefore reweight the data silently. Generating
prices and quantities together from the utility model keeps the shares
internally consistent.
}

